From 3266df0bdeb9d936a3c39fa4cb9a552e97f96409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:31:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Sleep between credential-export fixture gate checks

Avoid a continuously runnable filesystem polling loop while the export
subprocess waits for the same test fixture gate. Retain the 5000 ms export
deadline, ten-second coordination deadline, queued-caller assertion, and
all recovery and single-export assertions.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012).
Baseline: Windows job 119473329443 in run 39667622235 fails the existing
shared_bedrock_auth_refresh_is_reused_only_for_matching_configuration test
with an AWS credential export timeout after 5000 ms. Run 39633146357
reproduces the same outcome.

Verification: the maintained just fmt-check succeeds through the isolated
run-local-rust helper. Native repeated-test and full-matrix acceptance are
pending; this fixture change is a repair candidate, not proof of the
historical timeout's root cause.
---
 codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs b/codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs
index f8f0790..9ce7d63 100644
--- a/codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/model-provider/src/provider.rs
@@ -1038,7 +1038,7 @@ printf '%s\n' '{"AccessKeyId":"exported","SecretAccessKey":"secret"}'
                 result = &mut first_refresh => panic!("export should wait for its gate: {result:?}"),
                 () = async {
                     while !export_counter.exists() {
-                        tokio::task::yield_now().await;
+                        tokio::time::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(10)).await;
                     }
                 } => {}
             }
